the first tank plan, in full:
  1. Project skeleton and file map
     files: index.html, css/style.css, BRIEF.md
     Make index.html load css and game.js only; make css/style.css basic full-screen split layout. Add BRIEF.md listing planned files.
  2. Core game state and loop
     files: js/state.js, js/game.js, BRIEF.md, config/settings.js
     Create config values (arena size, tank speed, fire rate). state.js holds two players, positions, bullets, powerups; game.js runs the update/render loop in canvas.
  3. Render tanks and arena
     files: js/draw.js, css/style.css, index.html
     draw.js renders split-screen top-down tanks (two canvases), arena borders, and a temporary grid so walls can be seen later. Keep state untouched.
  4. Input for two players
     files: js/input.js, js/game.js
     Map WASD+Space for P1 and Arrows+Enter for P2. Input sets desired movement/fire flags on state, not canvas.
  5. Destructible walls
     files: js/levels.js, config/levels.js, js/draw.js, js/state.js
     Make levels.js load a simple tile map (wall/empty/indestructible) into state.walls. Provide function to remove a wall when a bullet hits it. Update draw to render wall types.
  6. Bullets and collisions
     files: js/collisions.js, js/game.js
     Move bullets by speed, collide with walls (destroy destructible tile), tanks (damage/hp), and arena edge. Tank death triggers respawn with hp loss.
  7. Power-ups
     files: js/powerups.js, config/settings.js, js/draw.js
     Power-ups spawn at random empty tiles: speed, rapid fire, shield, extra hp. They last 5 seconds, update in state, and draw overlays on tanks. Two players start at opposite sides.
  8. Win screen and restart
     files: js/game.js, css/style.css, index.html
     Track lives (default 3). When someone hits 0, show overlay text declaring winner, and allow pressing R to restart round. Must not touch powerups or wall logic.

